---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { PUBLISHER, SITE } from '../consts';
---
<Base title="Terms & Conditions"
      description="The terms on which App-Tipps.com is made available, including intellectual property, acceptable use, affiliate disclosure and limitation of liability.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="prose" style="padding:34px 0 10px">
      <h1>Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated 12 August 2026.</p>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        App-Tipps.com is operated by {PUBLISHER.legalName}, registered in England and Wales under number
        {' '}{PUBLISHER.companyNumber}, registered office {PUBLISHER.address.street}, {PUBLISHER.address.city}
        {' '}{PUBLISHER.address.postcode}, {PUBLISHER.address.country}. By using this site you accept these terms.
        If you do not accept them, please do not use the site.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Using the site</h2>
      <p>
        You may read, print and share our articles for your own personal, non-commercial use. You must not
        scrape the site, republish our articles in whole or in substantial part, use our content to train
        machine learning models without written permission, attempt to interfere with the site's operation,
        or use it for anything unlawful.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        All original text, photography, layout and branding on this site belongs to {PUBLISHER.legalName} or
        is used under licence. Game and app names, logos, screenshots and artwork belong to their respective
        owners and are used for the purpose of reporting and review. If you own material that appears here
        and want it removed, email us and we will act promptly.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Editorial content is opinion, not advice</h2>
      <p>
        Our reviews, scores and guides are our editorial judgement at the time of writing. Apps and games
        change constantly, and an article may be out of date. Nothing on this site is financial, legal,
        medical or professional advice. Decisions about what to download, buy or spend money on are yours.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Advertising and affiliate links</h2>
      <p>
        This site carries advertising and affiliate links. Where an article contains affiliate links, that
        is disclosed on the article. We may earn a commission on purchases made through those links, at no
        extra cost to you. Advertising does not influence our editorial judgement; see our
        {' '}<a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Third-party links</h2>
      <p>
        We link to app stores, developer sites and other publications. We do not control those sites and are
        not responsible for their content, their products or their privacy practices.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Availability and liability</h2>
      <p>
        We try to keep the site accurate and available but we do not guarantee either. To the fullest extent
        permitted by law, we exclude liability for any loss arising from your use of, or inability to use,
        this site or anything you obtained through it. Nothing in these terms excludes liability for death
        or personal injury caused by negligence, for fraud, or for anything else that cannot lawfully be
        excluded.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms. The version published at {SITE.url}/terms-and-conditions/ is the one that
        applies, and the date above shows when it last changed.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales, and the courts of England and Wales have
        exclusive jurisdiction, except that consumers resident elsewhere keep the benefit of any mandatory
        protections of their local law.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Contact</h2>
      <p><a href={`mailto:${PUBLISHER.editorialEmail}`}>{PUBLISHER.editorialEmail}</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
